## Known caveats carried forward

- Fresh GitHub uploads may not immediately propagate consistently through all GitHub views.
- Mock/sandbox tests do not prove native/model behavior.
- A real-runtime `[SMOKE SETUP FAILURE]` means the local test tree cannot resolve `node-llama-cpp` from `llama_worker/llama.mjs`; it is not a runtime behavior result.
- Real-runtime output warnings in `smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs` are not default failures unless strict flags are enabled.
- Prior broad command wrapper timeouts around slow lifecycle/native-policy smoke suites should be isolated before being classified as deterministic behavior failures.

## Recommended next work after closeout

After Worker Layout Option C finalization is staged, tested, artifact-guarded, GitHub-verified, and checkpointed, the next separate branch family is parent-runtime lifecycle modularization.

Likely next branch:

```text
runtime-lifecycle-modularization-v1-request-settlement-helper
```

That branch must begin with a fresh source review and a settlement matrix from current parent-runtime request settlement paths. Do not combine it with Worker Option C finalization.
